  "body": "Some properties are difficult to compare. This is one of them.\r\n\r\nArchitectural individuality, substantial concrete construction, established rental income and remarkable flexibility come together in a residence that occupies a category of its own. Our clients are committed to achieving a sale and invite genuine proposals from buyers prepared to recognise its value.\r\n\r\nPositioned within one of Devonport's tightly held coastal enclaves, this distinctive European-inspired residence offers an opportunity to acquire something genuinely different from the conventional property offering.\r\n\r\nThere is also an unusual degree of flexibility around the purchase itself. For the right purchaser, our clients are prepared to consider trade proposals involving residential property, vehicles, boats, silver or a considered combination of assets alongside a cash component. Every genuine proposal will be considered.\r\n\r\nCurrently tenanted and generating $2,140 per week, equivalent to $111,280 per annum, the property provides an established income stream from day one, while offering future options for an owner occupier, investor or purchaser seeking a combination of home and income.\r\n\r\nExperience the residence through the cinematic VIDEO TOUR and explore its architectural detail and multi-level configuration in the interactive 3D VIRTUAL TOUR, accessible via the box icon.\r\n\r\nBelieved to be one of only two European-inspired homes of its kind, this remarkable residence has a presence that is immediately apparent. Constructed during the 1990s in solid concrete, its European loft-inspired aesthetic is defined by soaring stud heights, exposed timber beams, extensive glazing, bespoke joinery and natural materials. Substantial, expressive and distinctive, it has been designed with a sense of permanence.\r\n\r\nAcross three levels, the accommodation offers exceptional versatility. The independently accessed ground floor is configured as a self-contained two bedroom space, complete with open-plan living, kitchen and bathroom facilities. Together with the light business zoning, this level offers scope for rental accommodation, executive living, consulting or a professional home-based practice.\r\n\r\nThe middle level forms the social heart of the home. Generous proportions, extensive glazing and a wood-burning fireplace create a welcoming environment, with elevated outlooks across Waitemata Golf Course bringing greenery and natural light into the living spaces. Above, the upper level provides a more private retreat, able to function independently or as an extension of the principal residence.\r\n\r\nFor investors, the current tenancy provides established income. For owner occupiers, the opportunity to combine substantial living accommodation with an income-producing or independently accessed space is particularly appealing. Extended families and business owners will also appreciate the separation and flexibility across the three levels.\r\n\r\nBeyond the residence, Devonport offers a lifestyle that remains difficult to replicate. Village cafes and restaurants, ferry connections to the CBD, waterfront walks, beaches, reserves, premium schooling and Mount Victoria are all within easy reach.\r\n\r\nWhat sets this property apart is the combination of qualities rarely found together: distinctive architecture, concrete construction, established income, flexible accommodation and a sought-after coastal location.\r\n\r\nIf you recognise the opportunity, we welcome your inspection and a considered proposal. Whether your interest is investment, owner occupation or a creative acquisition arrangement, our clients are open to a conversation and prepared to consider the possibilities.\r\n\r\nA distinctive Devonport residence. An established income. A flexible approach to purchase.\r\n\r\nProudly presented by The EK Group, delivering prestige, passion, and property without parallel.",
